{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>Jacob has taken all that belongs to our father.</b> And afterward they said, ״וּמֵאֲשֶׁר לְאָבִינוּ עָשָׂה אֵת כָּל הַכָּבוֹד הַזֶּה״ — 'מִן' implies part of what, not all of what, and if so, their words contradict each other. And even without that, it is difficult: how could they say so blatant a falsehood — did Jacob really take all that belongs to their father, and did he leave him nothing at all? Laban still had sheep and cattle and tents. And the explanation of the matter is thus: that at first they were not speaking against the property at all, but rather against the schemes and matters of deceit in which their father was expert beyond everyone in the world, so that he could deceive others but others could not deceive him. And Jacob learned from Laban all of his deceit, to the point that even Laban could not stand before him, for he outwitted Laban. And concerning this they said, 'Jacob has taken all that belongs to our father' — he took all of his deceit from him. And concerning the property they said, 'and from what belongs to our father he has made all this glory.'"], :book :genesis, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:31:15.042942394Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}